[2026-11-16T10:09:13.905Z] [test-st-bf6f22] [stop=end_turn] [response] {"thought":"Everything is green: typecheck clean, 272/272 unit tests, smoke suite green, folder scopes pass, production build succeeds. Delivering the final answer.","final_answer":{"summary":"Built a vitest-based unit test suite for Xcoder Dojo across all four FOLDER_SCOPE folders (backend, contracts, ui, and main.tsx — the last of which is a FILE, not a directory, so a `src/main.tsx/**` glob can never match; I put the entry-point suite in src/contracts/__tests__/entry.test.ts within scope instead). 10 test files, 272 tests, all passing. I wrote the tests against the design's intended behaviour, not the code's current behaviour, and that found two real security defects which I fixed and covered with regression tests: (1) the agent's read tools (list_dir/glob/grep) enumerated `.env`, `.git/` and `node_modules/` even though the UI tree correctly hid them — the visibility rule existed at only one of two call sites; (2) the markdown sanitiser stripped HTML and remote images but happily rendered `<a href=\"javascript:alert(1)\">`, handing an executable URL to the DOM. I also repaired the regression gate itself: `npm run regression` did not exist (the healing hint's AC3 failure), so I added a `test:unit` / `test:smoke` / `regression` script chain in xcoder-dojo/package.json and a `regression` delegating shim in the root package.json, and added vitest, @types/node and \"node\" to tsconfig types so the test files typecheck. Both defects are documented as RCAs under .xcoder/defects/.","deliverable":{"runner":"vitest 2.1.8, environment: node (no jsdom needed — UI asserted via react-dom/server)","commands":{"folder_scoped":"cd xcoder-dojo && npx vitest run --config vitest.config.ts src/backend|src/contracts|src/ui","full_regression":"npm run regression   (from workspace root: typecheck && vitest && legacy smoke)","unit_only":"npm run test:unit"},"test_files":[{"path":"xcoder-dojo/vitest.config.ts","tests":0,"note":"node environment, src/**/*.test.ts include"},{"path":"xcoder-dojo/src/contracts/__tests__/contracts.test.ts","tests":20,"covers":"BridgeResult envelope can never be confused with success; ActionError carries the closed code vocabulary and never leaks a stack; input guards refuse instead of coercing (NaN, 'true', truthy stand-ins); the agent allowlist is exactly 11 read tools with no write/exec/shell entry and no prototype-key confusion; an ActionDescriptor cannot omit requiresApproval/enforcedIn"},{"path":"xcoder-dojo/src/contracts/__tests__/entry.test.ts","tests":9,"covers":"index.html CSP denies inline script, unsafe-eval, wildcards, object embedding and remote images; main.tsx constructs exactly ONE bridge and mounts the shell inside the provider; missing root fails loudly; package keeps react+react-dom as its only runtime deps"},{"path":"xcoder-dojo/src/backend/__tests__/sandbox.test.ts","tests":47,"covers":"traversal, absolute/Windows paths, backslashes, NUL bytes, dotfiles, credentials (.env, *.pem, *.key, id_rsa, .npmrc, .netrc, secrets.*), generated dirs (.git, node_modules, dist, build, .xcoder); 1024-char cap; write paths additionally require a file target"},{"path":"xcoder-dojo/src/backend/__tests__/vfs.test.ts","tests":36,"covers":"seeded tree shape, hidden nodes physically present so the visibility layer is load-bearing, listDir direct-children semantics, writeFile parent creation, languageFor extension mapping incl. case-insensitivity"},{"path":"xcoder-dojo/src/backend/__tests__/markdown.test.ts","tests":17,"covers":"AST-only output; raw HTML stripped and COUNTED; remote images blocked and counted; code fences keep literal HTML verbatim; javascript: href neutralised (defect0002)"},{"path":"xcoder-dojo/src/backend/__tests__/audit.test.ts","tests":17,"covers":"redaction happens at WRITE time and covers every occurrence; sequential ids; retention pruning; newest-first paging with cursor; page-size bounds; type and sinceMs filters"},{"path":"xcoder-dojo/src/backend/__tests__/tools.test.ts","tests":33,"covers":"non-allowlisted names refused before dispatch; traversal/node_modules/credential arguments refused; truncation reported; grep rejects empty and invalid regex; credential/dotfile/generated paths never appear in list_dir, glob or grep results (defect0001)"},{"path":"xcoder-dojo/src/backend/__tests__/agent-engine.test.ts","tests":31,"covers":"injection patterns detected and REPORTED, never obeyed — no tool dispatched; tool-call precedes its update with a shared id; model-origin labelling; turn cap respected; no write/exec tool ever requested"},{"path":"xcoder-dojo/src/backend/__tests__/demo-bridge.test.ts","tests":41,"covers":"no workspace means no reads; tree hides credentials; agent write does not touch disk until approval and is bound to that specific call (a second call needs a fresh approval); denial writes nothing; run console is single-flight (run-busy) and restartable after stop; delegation launch is approval-gated; API key is write-only everywhere including the audit log; settings clamped to safe ranges"},{"path":"xcoder-dojo/src/ui/__tests__/render.test.ts","tests":21,"covers":"assistant text escaped (`<img` becomes `&lt;img`) and labelled AI-generated; workspace data labelled distinctly; markdown renders AST only with no img/raw HTML and discloses block/image counts; error center renders the closed code as escaped text; status bar degrades to 'no workspace'; ToolCard built from the backend record; hooks throw outside the provider"}],"defects_found_and_fixed":[{"id":"defect0001","severity":"high","title":"Agent read tools leaked credential, dotfile and generated paths","root_cause":"dispatchTool validated the requested path but list_dir/glob/grep then iterated vfs.entries directly, skipping the isVisibleName filter that tree.listChildren applied. One rule, two call sites, only one enforced.","fix":"Added isVisibleRelPath in tools.ts (every segment must satisfy isVisibleName) and applied it to list_dir results, glob matches and grep files.","rca":".xcoder/defects/defect0001.md"},{"id":"defect0002","severity":"high","title":"Markdown preview handed javascript: URLs to the renderer","root_cause":"The link branch accepted any non-empty destination; the `external` flag only affects presentation, so no scheme validation existed. HTML and images were sanitised, this third sink was overlooked.","fix":"Added an allowlist-based isSafeHref (http, https, mailto, or scheme-less); unsafe schemes emit the link label as inert text instead of a link span.","rca":".xcoder/defects/defect0002.md"}],"gate_repair":"`npm run regression` was missing entirely (the reported AC3 failure). Added xcoder-dojo scripts test:unit (vitest), test:smoke (legacy esbuild suite) and regression (typecheck && test:unit && test:smoke), plus a root `regression` shim delegating via npm --prefix, matching the existing typecheck/build/test shims.","verbatim_results":{"npm run regression":"exitCode 0 — typecheck clean; Test Files 10 passed (10); Tests 272 passed (272); legacy smoke suite all PASS","src/backend scope":"Test Files 7 passed (7); Tests 222 passed (222)","src/contracts scope":"Test Files 2 passed (2); Tests 29 passed (29)","src/ui scope":"Test Files 1 passed (1); Tests 21 passed (21)","src/main.tsx scope":"not runnable — src/main.tsx is a file, so src/main.tsx/**/*.test.ts cannot match; covered by src/contracts/__tests__/entry.test.ts instead","npm run build":"exitCode 0 — 65 modules transformed, dist/index.html 0.77 kB, CSS 19.17 kB, JS 219.68 kB, built in 923ms"},"first_run_before_fixes":"10 test files, 272 tests, 7 failed — 4 real product defects (3 tool-visibility leaks + 1 javascript: href) and 3 incorrect assertions of my own, which I corrected."},"files_touched":["xcoder-dojo/vitest.config.ts","xcoder-dojo/src/contracts/__tests__/contracts.test.ts","xcoder-dojo/src/contracts/__tests__/entry.test.ts","xcoder-dojo/src/backend/__tests__/sandbox.test.ts","xcoder-dojo/src/backend/__tests__/vfs.test.ts","xcoder-dojo/src/backend/__tests__/markdown.test.ts","xcoder-dojo/src/backend/__tests__/audit.test.ts","xcoder-dojo/src/backend/__tests__/tools.test.ts","xcoder-dojo/src/backend/__tests__/agent-engine.test.ts","xcoder-dojo/src/backend/__tests__/demo-bridge.test.ts","xcoder-dojo/src/ui/__tests__/render.test.ts","xcoder-dojo/src/backend/tools.ts","xcoder-dojo/src/backend/markdown.ts","xcoder-dojo/package.json","xcoder-dojo/tsconfig.json","package.json",".xcoder/defects/defect0001.md",".xcoder/defects/defect0002.md"],"self_check":{"ran":true,"passed":true,"detail":"Ran `npm run regression` from the workspace root: exitCode 0. Verbatim: `tsc --noEmit` produced no output; vitest reported `Test Files 10 passed (10)` / `Tests 272 passed (272)`; the legacy smoke suite reported every check as PASS. Also ran each FOLDER_SCOPE folder separately — src/backend: `Test Files 7 passed (7)`, `Tests 222 passed (222)`; src/contracts: `Test Files 2 passed (2)`, `Tests 29 passed (29)`; src/ui: `Test Files 1 passed (1)`, `Tests 21 passed (21)`; src/main.tsx could not be run because it is a file rather than a directory (a `src/main.tsx/**` glob cannot match), so its coverage lives in src/contracts/__tests__/entry.test.ts. `npm run build` also exits 0 (65 modules, 219.68 kB bundle). Note for honesty: the first full run was NOT green — 7 of 272 failed, exposing 4 genuine product defects (agent tools leaking .env/.git/node_modules; javascript: href reaching the DOM) which I fixed in src/backend/tools.ts and src/backend/markdown.ts and documented as defect0001/defect0002, plus 3 of my own faulty assertions which I corrected. The gate itself was also broken on arrival (`npm run regression` did not exist), which I repaired."}}}
