[2026-11-16T10:16:09.552Z] [test-st-bf6f22] [stop=end_turn] [response] Now I'll patch the interface to carry the timer handle.\n\n{\n  "thought": "Add an optional timer handle to ApprovalTicket so both the expiry path and the respond path can clear it.",\n  "action": {\n    "tool": "edit_file",\n    "input": {\n      "path": "xcoder-dojo/src/backend/demo-bridge.ts",\n      "old_str": "  expiresAtMs: number;\n  resolve: (decision: 'approved' | 'denied' | 'expired') => void;\n}",\n      "new_str": "  expiresAtMs: number;\n  resolve: (decision: 'approved' | 'denied' | 'expired') => void;\n  /**\n   * Handle for the expiry timer. Tracked so every resolution path can clear it;\n   * otherwise a resolved approval leaves a 120s timer holding the event loop\n   * open and a Node process (e.g. the smoke test) never exits.\n   */\n  timer?: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>;\n}"\n    }\n  }\n}
